Feature: Advice for the commander
  A commander can have an [[advisor]] that helps it. The advisor looks at the map of the team,
  like the commander, and sends a [[proposal]] when it sees a better move: an order for a drone, the points that it expects
  to gain by it, and the time after which it is stale. The advisor does not give orders. The
  commander decides.

  The computer commander takes a proposal when it gains more than 2 points, when it is not
  stale, and when it still fits: the drone is free to take an order, and the tower is not one
  that the team holds now. Of the proposals that it can take, it takes the one that gains most.
  A proposal that does not fit is dropped.

  The first advisor is the lookahead. Every 5 s it plays the game forward 45 s in a small model.
  The enemy drones in the model are guesses from its [[belief]]. It tries to send each free
  drone to each other tower, and proposes the change that gives most points. Its proposal is
  good for 45 s. A commander with no advisor does not think ahead. A commander thinks ahead
  with the lookahead by default.

  An advisor can be slow. Its proposals then reach the commander some seconds after the map
  that it looked at. A proposal that arrives after its time is stale, and the commander does
  not take it.

  Expectation: A proposal that gains enough is taken
    The advisor proposes that the first Blue drone takes the Red home tower, for 5 points. At the
    start the commander sends the first drone to the west tower.

    Given the proposal in the hand of the Blue commander is the Red home tower for 5 points
    When the computer commander of Blue weighs the proposal
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the Red home tower

  Expectation: A proposal that gains little is not taken
    The commander takes a proposal only when it gains more than 2 points.

    Given the proposal in the hand of the Blue commander is the Red home tower for 1 point
    When the computer commander of Blue weighs the proposal
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower

  Expectation: A stale proposal is not taken
    The proposal is good for 5 s. The commander decides 10 s later, and does what it does with no
    proposal: at that time it sends the first drone to the centre tower.

    Given the proposal in the hand of the Blue commander is the Red home tower for 5 points, good for 5 seconds
    When the computer commander of Blue weighs the proposal 10 seconds later
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the centre tower

  Expectation: A proposal for a tower that the team holds now is not taken
    The advisor looked at the map when the Red home tower was Red's. When the commander decides,
    Blue holds it.

    Given the towers held by Blue are 2
    And the west tower is neutral
    And the Red home tower is held by Blue
    And the proposal in the hand of the Blue commander is the Red home tower for 5 points, from the map of 3 seconds before
    When the computer commander of Blue weighs the proposal
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower

  Expectation: A commander with no advisor does not think ahead
    Overrides: The commander does not keep a drone at a tower that the enemy holds with two drones
    The west tower is Red's, and two Red drones circle it. A commander that thinks ahead sends
    the first drone to a free tower, as in [[The computer commander]]. A commander with no
    advisor does not.

    Given the advisor of the computer commander of Blue is none
    And the west tower is held by Red
    And the control of the west tower is -100 %
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 2
    And the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the first Blue drone is 190 m from the centre tower
    When the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
